.TH MUSIC-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-17" "music-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
music-revamped \- now playing in the tmux status bar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B music-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ name ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B music-revamped
shows the track that is playing, its state, a progress bar and its times in
the tmux status line, and binds keys that play, pause and skip. The track
comes from the first source present: nowplaying-cli on macOS, playerctl when
a player answers it, cmus, then Spotify through osascript on macOS. With
playerctl the player that is playing wins, and the keys act on that player.
.PP
The entry point
.B music-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, which binds the menu key and every other key
that is set, in one tmux call, and replaces the placeholders #{music},
#{music_icon}, #{music_status}, #{music_title}, #{music_artist},
#{music_progress} and #{music_time} in status-left and status-right.
.PP
A status call prints the stored reading at once. When that reading is older
than the interval it starts one reading in the background, so the status line
never waits. A key with no player to control says so in a tmux message. Run
with no command on a terminal, the tool offers a menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Bind the keys and replace the status placeholders now. In the options render mode it also starts the daemon.
.TP
.B list
Print every tmux command apply would send, one per line, and change nothing.
.TP
.B status
Print one placeholder from the stored reading: now, icon, status, title, artist, progress or time. The status line runs it, and it starts a reading in the background when the stored one is older than the interval.
.TP
.B refresh
Read the player now, store the reading for the status line, and say what is playing.
.TP
.B play-pause
Play or pause the player.
.TP
.B next
Skip to the next track.
.TP
.B prev
Go back to the previous track.
.TP
.B daemon
Read the player and publish every placeholder the status line uses, once per interval, until another daemon takes over or the tmux server ends. apply starts it in the options render mode.
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux, the player it reads, the player it controls, the keys it found bound, gum and the core tools.
A settings row names any setting whose value it does not know.
Exits 1 only when a required tool is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B list
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.TP
.BI \-\- setting " value"
Any tmux option below, named with dashes, such as
.B \-\-interval
or
.BR \-\-max\-len .
It also takes the form
.IR \-\-setting = value ,
and outranks the environment and the tmux option. Given to
.BR apply ,
it rides on every binding, every menu item and every status call.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BI MUSIC_REVAMPED_ SETTING
Any tmux option below in capitals, such as
.BR MUSIC_REVAMPED_INTERVAL .
It outranks the tmux option.
.TP
.B MUSIC_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B MUSIC_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B MUSIC_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B MUSIC_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
An empty tmux option means its default. A key set to off binds nothing.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_menu_key
The prefix key that opens the playback menu. off binds nothing. The default is M\-m, left alone when someone else holds it.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_playpause_key
The prefix key that plays or pauses. The default is none.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_next_key
The prefix key that skips to the next track. The default is none.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_prev_key
The prefix key that goes back to the previous track. The default is none.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_interval
Seconds a reading stays fresh before the player is read again. The default is 5.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_format
The printf format for the title and the artist in #{music}. The default is %s \- %s.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_max_len
Cut the title and the artist to this many characters and add three dots. 0 keeps them whole. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_before
Text placed before #{music} when there is a track to show. The default is none.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_after
Text placed after #{music} when there is a track to show. The default is none.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_auto_hide
1 hides the icon unless a track is playing or paused. 0 always shows it. The default is 1.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_playing_icon
The icon while playing. The default is >.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_paused_icon
The icon while paused. The default is ||.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_stopped_icon
The icon while stopped. The default is [].
.TP
.B @music_revamped_unknown_icon
The icon when the state is unknown. The default is none.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_progress_width
Cells in the progress bar. The default is 10, and 200 at most.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_progress_full
The filled cell of the progress bar. The default is a full block.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_progress_empty
The empty cell of the progress bar. The default is a light shade.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_time_format
The printf format for elapsed and total time. The default is %s/%s.
.TP
.B @music_revamped_render
jobs turns each placeholder into a call the status line runs. options turns it into a read of a tmux option that the daemon fills, so a status refresh starts no process. The default is jobs.
.TP
.B @revamped_theme
The theme of every tmux-revamped tool, when nothing else sets one. The default
is
.BR kodougu .
.PP
The stored reading lives in
.BR @music_revamped_status ,
.BR _status_ts ,
.BR _status_lock ,
.BR _title ,
.BR _artist ,
.B _position
and
.BR _duration .
apply records the placeholders the status line uses in
.BR @music_revamped_published ,
the daemon writes each one to
.BI @music_revamped_out_ name
and keeps its process id in
.BR @music_revamped_ticker_pid .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR playerctl (1),
.BR cmus\-remote (1),
.BR gum (1)
